{"study_accession":"PRJNA1031175","secondary_study_accession":"SRP468030","title":"Inflammasome-resistant IPSC-derived myeloid-derived suppressor cells (iMDSCs) ameliorate xenogeneic GVHD","description":"Acute graft versus host disease (aGVHD) is considered a major complication of allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant (aHSCT). Front-line pharmaceutical treatment is not uniformly effective and has toxic side effects. Myeloid-derived suppressor cells (MDSCs) are a heterogeneous population of immature myeloid cells with potent immunosuppressive functions. Their potential to control GVHD has been proven in different rodent models. However, a high MDSC to T cell ratio and multiple doses of MDSCs are needed to achieve maximum effectiveness. Clinical translation of in vitro MDSC generation limits its clinical usage by a relatively low yield and need for personalized patient products, especially challenging for multiple treatment courses. Therefore, we developed an in vitro method to generate MDSCs on a large scale from a human induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC)-derived CD34+ cells. iMDSCs shared a similar morphology, phenotype, and suppressive function with peripheral blood (PB)-MDSCs. In striking contrast to PB-MDSCs, iMDSCs retained 95% of suppressor function when exposed to the damage-associated molecular pattern stimuli, LPS + ATP, released during GVHD. RNAseq analysis and gene knockdown studies revealed that inflammasome-resistant iMDSCs maintained expression of phosphoglycerate dehydrogenase, an enzyme involved in purine metabolism. Consistent with the retention of suppressor function during lethal xenogeneic GVHD-induced tissue injury, recipients of human iMDSCs and peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) experienced therapeutic benefits. Together, these data provide a platform for translating in vitro generated, off-the-shelf iMDSCs into the clinic for suppressing GVHD and other adverse immune responses. Overall design: Human myeloid derived suppressor cells were differentiated from PBMC and iPSC. For inflammasome study, PBMC derived MDSCs (PB MDSC) and iPSC derived MDSCs (iMDSC) were treated with/without LPS and ATP to induce the inflammasome and then frozen down with lysis buffer for RNAseq. For iMDSCs subtypes(CD14- vs CD14+) comparison, cells were flow sorted by the CD14 expression and frozen down with lysis buffer for RNAseq.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN37931601","study_accession":"PRJNA1031175","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMDSC_4 (3409)","description":"PBMDSC_4 (3409)","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7854508","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":4,"first_public":"2025-10-23","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","PBMC derived MDSC"],["genotype","WT"],["treatment","Non treated"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR26484081","experiment_accession":"SRX22187973","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":4687007,"base_count":712425064,"first_public":"2025-10-23","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7854508: PBMDSC_4 (3409) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR26484082","experiment_accession":"SRX22187973","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":4621569,"base_count":702478488,"first_public":"2025-10-23","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7854508: PBMDSC_4 (3409) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR26484083","experiment_accession":"SRX22187973","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":4780745,"base_count":726673240,"first_public":"2025-10-23","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7854508: PBMDSC_4 (3409) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR26484084","experiment